    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners Doherty Buggy are delighted to bring this well-proportioned three bedroomed, three-storey terraced property to the market.  The property is superbly located in the heart of New Ross with views of the river Barrow.\r\n\r\nNumber 11 North Quay offers spacious and light-filled versatile residential accommodation laid out over three levels which extends to approximately 78.Sq. M. / 839 Sq. Ft. \r\n\r\nThe layout on ground floor comprises: open plan Living / Dining / Kitchen spanning the full depth of the property.  A staircase gives access to the first floor.  The layout at first floor level comprises of landing with staircase to second floor, bedroom one and a shower room.  The layout on the second floor comprises: landing area and two bedrooms.\r\n\r\nThe property provides a practical layout with excellent use of space throughout. The accommodation offers a good balance of living and bedroom areas, making it an ideal choice for a variety of purchasers, including first-time buyers, families and investors.\r\n\r\nThe three-storey configuration provides a sense of separation between the different areas of the home, while the three-bedroom accommodation offers flexibility for family living or a home office. The property presents an opportunity for a purchaser looking to acquire a well-sized home with scope to personalise to their own taste and requirements.\r\n\r\n\r\nNew Ross has an excellent choice of both primary and secondary schools including: Catherine McAuley Primary School, New Ross Educate Together National School and St. Canice's National School, Rosbercon.  The Secondary schools including St Mary’s Secondary Schools, Our Lady of Lourdes Secondary School, Good Counsel College, CBS Secondary School and Kennedy College Secondary School.\r\n\r\nNew Ross has an excellent choice of shopping facilities including Tesco Superstore, Supervalu, Lidl and Aldi.  There is an excellent choice of coffee houses, restaurants and public houses.  \r\n\r\nNew Ross is convenient to Waterford city, Kilkenny city and Wexford town.  A thirty-minute drive (via N25) will take you to Waterford City. A forty-five-minute drive (via R700) will take you to Kilkenny City.  The travelling time to Wexford town is thirty-five minutes (via N25).  The travelling time to Dublin by car is two-hours (via M9 or M11 motorways).\r\n\r\nNew Ross has excellent amenities including The Apex Sports, Health & Leisure Centre, New Ross Boat Club, New Ross Rugby Club, New Ross Golf Club.  The property is a five-minute walk over the bridge to the start of the South-East Greenway.  The other important amenities include Brandon House Hotel and Spa and New Ross Community Hospital along with a choice of Medical Practices.  \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
